# nr-office-pdf-writer: what the lead applies (all of it is in files this task does not own)

Not compiled: cargo was not run (the lead compiles the wave). The recording was produced by running Node (pdf-writer.mjs over
pdf-lib, reader pdf-analysis.mjs) once with the recorder; the Rust code in native/core/crates/mixdog-office-pdf/src/writer/ and
tests/twin_writer.rs has not been built.

## 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-pdf/src/lib.rs

After `pub mod forms;` add:

    pub mod writer;

The writer is reached as `mixdog_office_pdf::writer::{create_pdf, create_chart_pdf, apply_document_properties, WriterError,
WriterResult}`; tests/twin_writer.rs uses exactly that path. Signatures the callers (the PDF author tools, the docx add_chart
path) use:

    create_pdf<P: WriteProof>(proof: &P, env: &FontEnv, svg_fonts: &SvgFonts, path: &str, spec: &Value) -> WriterResult<Value>
    create_chart_pdf<P: WriteProof>(proof: &P, env: &FontEnv, path: &str, block: &Value, width: f64, palette: Option<&Value>) -> WriterResult<Value>

`spec` is `{ blocks, fields, properties }` as Node's createPdf takes it; the results are Node's result objects. `env` is
`FontEnv::host()` in production (the system faces and MIXDOG_OCR_FONT) and `svg_fonts` the faces SVG logos are drawn with.
A refusal is a `WriterError` whose `message()` is the text Node's Error carries.

## 2. native/core/Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, mixdog-workspace-hack

Nothing: the module uses mixdog-fsio, mixdog-js, mixdog-office-base, mixdog-pdf, mixdog-raster and serde_json, all already
dependencies of mixdog-office-pdf; the tests use base64, mixdog-office-base (test-support), mixdog-pdf, mixdog-raster,
mixdog-fsio and mixdog-testkit, already dependencies or dev-dependencies of it. No new crate and no new workspace edge.

## 3. native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json

Index the new set `office-writer` (recorder benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-writer.mjs, 1 file, golden.json; the
set's own MANIFEST.json is written at native/core/fixtures/office-writer/MANIFEST.json) with the manifest tool that built the
other entries: `node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/verify-manifests.mjs --write-index`.

The embedded-face case reads native/core/fixtures/office-measure/faces/MiriamLibre-Regular.otf (already in the tree).

## 4. SERVICE_PENDING (compose_flip.rs)

Nothing: this task registers no protocol method.
